    "q-79141": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79141",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Determine the dimension of\n$\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
