    "q-34852": {
      "dom_id": "step-q34852",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Determine the dimension of\n$\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 16 & -12 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 16 & -12 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
